{"title":"Triangle Chapter Mathcounts","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Triangle Chapter Mathcounts is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=North_Carolina_MathCounts\" title=\"North Carolina MathCounts\">North Carolina MathCounts</a> chapter, consisting of competitors in Wake County. As one of the state's strongest chapters, it usually is responsible for the majority of the National team.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Top_5_.28State_Top_15.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Top_5_(State_Top_15)\">Top 5 (State Top 15)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Chapter_Mathcounts&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Top 5 (State Top 15)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>2020: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Brianzjk&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Brianzjk (page does not exist)\">Brian Zhang</a>(2), <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=C4raymond&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"C4raymond (page does not exist)\">Raymond Ge</a>(3), <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Eric_Wu&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Eric Wu (page does not exist)\">Eric Wu</a>(4), Edward Zhang(5), Brandon Yang(7)<br />\n2019: Minseok Eli Park (1), Sukrith Velmineti (3), <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Eric_Wu&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Eric Wu (page does not exist)\">Eric Wu</a> (3), Brian Zhang (2), Edward Zhang (12)<br />\n2018: Minseok Eli Park (11), Edward Zhang, Vibhu Subramani (7), Diya Tripathy, Kenan Hasanaliyev (10)<br />\n2017: Alvin Chen (6), Jeffrey Liu (5), Raghav Arun,&#160;?,&#160;?<br />\n2016: Jerry Zhao (1), Ben Wu (2) , Alvin Chen(6), Jeffery Liu(3?),&#160;?<br />\n2015: Jerry Zhao,&#160;?,&#160;?,&#160;?,&#160;?<br />\n2009: Calvin Deng(1),&#160;?,&#160;?,&#160;?,&#160;?<br />\n2008: Calvin Deng(1),&#160;?,&#160;?,&#160;?,&#160;?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Team\">Team</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Chapter_Mathcounts&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Team\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>2026: Mills Park Middle School<br />\n2025: Mills Park Middle School, Cary Academy<br />\n2024: Cary Academy<br />\n2023: Cary Academy<br />\n2022: Cary Academy<br />\n2021:&#160;???<br />\n2020: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Carnage_Mathcounts\" title=\"Carnage Mathcounts\">Carnage Middle School</a>, Raleigh <br />\n2019: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Carnage_Mathcounts\" title=\"Carnage Mathcounts\">Carnage Middle School</a>, Raleigh <br />\n2018: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Carnage_Mathcounts\" title=\"Carnage Mathcounts\">Carnage Middle School</a>, Raleigh <br />\n2017: Mills Park Middle School, Cary <br />\n2016: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Carnage_Mathcounts\" title=\"Carnage Mathcounts\">Carnage Middle School</a>, Raleigh <br />\n2015: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Carnage_Mathcounts\" title=\"Carnage Mathcounts\">Carnage Middle School</a>, Raleigh <br />\n2008: Ligon Middle<br />\n2009: Ligon Middle<br />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018112400\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.028 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 32/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17667:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018112400 and revision id 279678. Re